The height of $\triangle ABC$ is also equal to the height of $\triangle BEC$, so the base of $\triangle BEC$ is $4$. Using similar triangles, the base of $\triangle DRC$ is $4/2 = 2$. The height of $\triangle DRC$ is $3$, and its area is $(1/2)(2)(3) = \boxed{3}$.

