\end{align*}
Also, we know that the area of the smaller triangle is $\frac{s^2}{\sqrt{3}}$ squared inches, while the area of the larger one is $\frac{16 \cdot \frac{s^2}{\sqrt{3}}}{\sqrt{3}}$, which simplifies to $16s^2$ squared inches.

Therefore, we have the following equation relating $s$ and $l$: \begin{align*}
    \frac{s^2}{\sqrt{3}} &= \frac{16}{\sqrt{3}} \cdot \left(\frac{45-3s}{3}\right)^2 \\
    s^2 &= 16(45-3s)^2
