          &= \frac{4 \times 3}{2 \times 1 \times 2 \times 1} \\
          &= \boxed{6}
\end{align}

Finally, we'll find the total number of ways to choose 3 boys and 2 girls by multiplying the above results:
\begin{align}
Total~ways &= C(7, 3) \times C(4, 2) \\
               &= \frac{35}{6} \times 6 \\
